UNWIND [{start: {_id:694}, end: {_id:686}, properties:{evidence:"Gangliosides are a family of sialic acid containing glycosphingolipids, highly enriched in neuronal and glial membranes, where they play important roles for development, proliferation, differentiation and maintenance of neuronal tissues and cells. The ganglioside GM3 serves as a common precursor for the a- and b-series gangliosides. The GD3-synthase (GD3S) catalyzes the synthesis of GD3 by adding sialic acid to GM3, segregating the a- and b-series of gangliosides and therefore controlling the levels of the major brain gangliosides GM1, GD1a, GD1b and GT1b.", annotationSubgraph:["Sphingolipid metabolic subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Autonomic Fibers, Postganglionic"], pmid:"22470521", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22470521"}}] AS row
