matergic subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"20847424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20847424"}}, {start: {_id:3}, end: {_id:1903}, properties:{evidence:"Physiological levels of ABeta¸ also have trophic and neuroprotective actions in trophic deprived conditions [95]. Many ABeta¸ has a physiological role in normal synapse function. In organotypic hippocampal slices, BACE activity is increased by synaptic activity and the resulting ABeta¸ peptides depress excitatory transmission through a-amino-3-hydroxyl-5-methyl-4-isoxazole-propionate (AMPA) and N-methyl-D-aspartic acid (NMDA) receptors, suggesting a role for ABeta¸ in homeostatic plasticity [29]. ABeta¸ may have an important physiological role in synapse elimination during brain development", annotationSubgraph:["Glutamatergic subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"20847424", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20847424"}}, {start: {_id:2263}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"Recent studies showed that melatonin, an indoleamine secreted by the pineal gland, may play an important/ role in aging and AD as an antioxidant and neuroprotector. Melatonin decreases during aging and patients with AD have a/ more profound reduction in this hormone.Melatonin efficiently protects neuronal cells from Abeta- mediated toxicity via/ antioxidant and anti-amyloid properties: it not only inhibits Abeta generation, but also arrests the formation of amyloid/ fibrils by a structure-dependent interaction with Abeta. Our recent studies have demonstrated that melatonin efficiently/ attenuates Alzheimer-like tau hyperphosphorylation. Although the exact mechanism is still not fully understood, a direct/ regulatory influence of melatonin on the activities of protein kinases and protein phosphatases is proposed. Additionally,/ melatonin also plays a role in protecting cholinergic neurons and in anti-inflammation.", annotationSubgraph:["Non-amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16364209", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16364209"}}, {start: {_id:2263}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Recent studies showed that melatonin, an indoleamine secreted by the pineal gland, may play an important/ role in aging and AD as an antioxidant and neuroprotector. Melatonin decreases during aging and patients with AD have a/ more profound reduction in this hormone.Melatonin efficiently protects neuronal cells from Abeta- mediated toxicity via/ antioxidant and anti-amyloid properties: it not only inhibits Abeta generation, but also arrests the formation of amyloid/ fibrils by a structure-dependent interaction with Abeta. Our recent studies have demonstrated that melatonin efficiently/ attenuates Alzheimer-like tau hyperphosphorylation. Although the exact mechanism is still not fully understood, a direct/ regulatory influence of melatonin on the activities of protein kinases and protein phosphatases is proposed. Additionally,/ melatonin also plays a role in protecting cholinergic neurons and in anti-inflammation.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Very High"], pmid:"16364209", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16364209"}}, {start: {_id:4132}, end: {_id:4135}, properties:{evidence:"Gen also significantly reversed Abeta25-35-induced up-regulation of TLR4 and NF-ÎºB expression and the DNA binding and transcriptional activities of NF-ÎºB.These results indicated that Gen could alleviate the inflammation caused by Abeta25-35 treatment, which might be associated with the regulation of the TLR4/NF-ÎºB signal pathway.", annotationSubgraph:["Inflammatory response subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Inflammation"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Microglia"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"24290604", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24290604"}}, {start: {_id:4153}, end: {_id:97}, properties:{evidence:"The caspase-1 inhibitor Z-YVAD-FMK inhibits the processing of IL-1beta, and attenuates microglial neurotoxicity.", annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"24357806", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24357806"}}, {start: {_id:4188}, end: {_id:4189}, properties:{evidence:"Results of this study indicate that ethanol extracts of SF (SF-E) suppress NMDA-induced reactive oxygen species (ROS) production in neurons, and LPS- and IFNgamma-induced ROS and nitric oxide (NO) production in microglial cells.", annotationSubgraph:["Reactive oxygen species subgraph", "Interferon signaling subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Microglia"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"24587007", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24587007"}}, {start: {_id:4188}, end: {_id:4190}, properties:{evidence:"Results of this study indicate that ethanol extracts of SF (SF-E) suppress NMDA-induced reactive oxygen species (ROS) production in neurons, and LPS- and IFNgamma-induced ROS and nitric oxide (NO) production in microglial cells.", annotationSubgraph:["Interferon signaling subgraph", "Nitric oxide subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Microglia"], annotationConfidence:["Low"], pmid:"24587007", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24587007"}}, {start: {_id:4268}, end: {_id:2459}, properties:{evidence:"Additionally, CDT also inhibited the increase of TNF-Î± and IL-6 level, and increased the expression of choline acetyltransferase (ChAT), receptor of activated protein kinase C1 (RACK1) and brain- derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF) in brain as compared to model mice.", annotationSpecies:["10090"], annotationMeshdisease:["Memory Disorders"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Brain"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"24422705", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24422705"}}, {start: {_id:4268}, end: {_id:4269}, properties:{evidence:"Additionally, CDT also inhibited the increase of TNF-Î± and IL-6 level, and increased the expression of choline acetyltransferase (ChAT), receptor of activated protein kinase C1 (RACK1) and brain- derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF) in brain as compared to model mice.", annotationSpecies:["10090"], annotationMeshdisease:["Memory Disorders"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Brain"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"24422705", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24422705"}}, {start: {_id:4286}, end: {_id:2029}, properties:{evidence:"Furthermore, XD4 significantly inhibits Abeta oligomer-induced cytotoxicity to glial cells and decreases the production of proinflammatory cytokines, such as TNF-Î± and IL-1beta, in vitro and in vivo.", annotationSubgraph:["Interleukin signaling subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Neuroglia"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], citationType:"PubMed Central", citationRef:"PMC3981768"}}, {start: {_id:4286}, end: {_id:2459}, properties:{evidence:"Furthermore, XD4 significantly inhibits Abeta oligomer-induced cytotoxicity to glial cells and decreases the production of proinflammatory cytokines, such as TNF-Î± and IL-1beta, in vitro and in vivo.", annotationSubgraph:["Tumor necrosis factor subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Neuroglia"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], citationType:"PubMed Central", citationRef:"PMC3981768"}}, {start: {_id:4319}, end: {_id:4190}, properties:{evidence:"Nicardipine also significantly inhibited LPS plus IFN-gamma-induced release of nitric oxide (NO), and the expression of inducible nitric oxide synthase (iNOS) and cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2).", annotationSubgraph:["Interferon signaling subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"24621589", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24621589"}}, {start: {_id:4319}, end: {_id:2493}, properties:{evidence:"Nicardipine also significantly inhibited LPS plus IFN-gamma-induced release of nitric oxide (NO), and the expression of inducible nitric oxide synthase (iNOS) and cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2).", annotationSubgraph:["Nitric oxide subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"24621589", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24621589"}}, {start: {_id:4319}, end: {_id:4277}, properties:{evidence:"Nicardipine also significantly inhibited LPS plus IFN-gamma-induced release of nitric oxide (NO), and the expression of inducible nitric oxide synthase (iNOS) and cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2).", annotationSubgraph:["Nitric oxide subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"24621589", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24621589"}}, {start: {_id:4321}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"Rutin improves spatial memory in Alzheimer's disease transgenic mice by reducing Abeta oligomer level and attenuating oxidative stress and neuroinflammation.", annotationSubgraph:["Non-amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["10090"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"24512768", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"24512768"}}] AS row
