edium"], pmid:"15211591", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"15211591"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"Preventing Abeta42 production with an M596I mutation (beta-), which blocks beta-secretase cleavage of APP, or by treatment with a gamma- secretase inhibitor increased the resistance of APP(FAD)-expressing cells to apoptotic process.", annotationSubgraph:["Beta secretase subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"15584903", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"15584903"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"Here, we established a novel approach to regulate production of Abeta based on intracellular expression of single chain antibodies (intrabodies) raised to an epitope adjacent to the beta-secretase cleavage site of human APP.", annotationSubgraph:["Beta secretase subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Low"], pmid:"15767460", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"15767460"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"The aspartic protease beta-secretase (BACE) cleaves the amyloid precursor protein into a 42 residue beta-peptide, which is the principal biochemical marker of Alzheimer's disease.", annotationSubgraph:["Beta secretase subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16216580", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16216580"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"Using high-throughput siRNA screening technology, we assessed 15,200 genes for their role in Abeta42 secretion and identified leucine-rich repeat transmembrane 3 (LRRTM3) as a neuronal gene that promotes APP processing by BACE1. siRNAs targeting LRRTM3 inhibit the secretion of Abeta40, Abeta42, and sAPPbeta, the N-terminal APP fragment produced by BACE1 cleavage, from cultured cells and primary neurons by up to 60%, whereas overexpression increases Abeta secretion.", annotationSubgraph:["Beta secretase subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Very High"], pmid:"17098871", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"17098871"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"After inhibitor treatment, the improved memory function was accompanied by reduced amyloid plaque load, decreased Abeta40 and Abeta42, and reduced C-terminal beta-secretase fragment derived from APP by beta-secretase.", pmid:"18184658", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"18184658"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:6}, properties:{evidence:"The novel transmembrane aspartic protease BACE (for Beta-site APP Cleaving Enzyme) is the beta-secretase that cleaves amyloid precursor protein to initiate beta-amyloid formation. As such, BACE is a prime therapeutic target for the treatment of Alzheimer's disease.", pmid:"10956649", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"10956649"}}] AS row
MATCH (start:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row.start._id})
