t GSK-3beta indeed phosphorylates MARK2, whereas it failed to phosphorylate Ser-262 of tau.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16257959", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16257959"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"In experimental pmodels of AD, GSK3B has been shown to hyperphosphorylate Tau, leading to microtubule disassembly and loss of function", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"20576277", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20576277"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Glycogen synthase kinase 3beta (GSK3beta) is a proline-directed kinase generally considered as one of the major players that (hyper)phosphorylates Tau.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"20679343", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20679343"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"The results provide initial evidence that TPKI/GSK-3 beta/FA after heparin potentiation may represent one of the most potent systems possibly involved in the abnormal phosphorylation of PHF-tau and neuronal degeneration in Alzheimer disease brains.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"7786411", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"7786411"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"A mixture of recombinant human tau isoforms phosphorylated by GSK-3 beta gave similar results to those obtained with control human brain tau.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"8050597", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"8050597"}}, {start: {_id:117}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Indirubins inhibit glycogen synthase kinase-3 beta and CDK5/p25, two protein kinases involved in abnormal tau phosphorylation in Alzheimer's disease.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Low"], pmid:"11013232", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"11013232"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:649}, properties:{evidence:"These results, respectively, indicated that GSK-3beta is responsible for phosphorylating Ser-262 of tau through phosphorylation and activation of MARK2 and that the phosphorylation of tau at this particular site is predominantly mediated by a GSK-3beta-MARK2 pathway.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16257959", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16257959"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:3111}, properties:{evidence:"These results, respectively, indicated that GSK-3beta is responsible for phosphorylating Ser-262 of tau through phosphorylation and activation of MARK2 and that the phosphorylation of tau at this particular site is predominantly mediated by a GSK-3beta-MARK2 pathway.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16257959", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16257959"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Glycogen synthase kinase-3beta phosphorylates protein tau and rescues the axonopathy in the central nervous system of human four-repeat tau transgenic mice.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"11007782", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"11007782"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Recent studies have shown that GSK-3beta phosphorylates the microtubule-associated protein tau in vitro and in cell culture.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"10486203", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"10486203"}}, {start: {_id:116}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Since prior phosphorylation of tau by TPKII strongly enhanced the action of TPKI, it was thought that TPKII was involved in the formation of PHF-tau in concert with TPKI.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Cyclin-CDK subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"9089387", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"9089387"}}] AS row
