ein (MAP) kinase SAPK/JNK phosphorylates tau protein at many of its proline-directed serine/threonine residues in vitro and is a likely candidate kinase to phosphorylate the pathologically relevant S422 site on tau.", annotationSubgraph:["MAPK-JNK subgraph", "Tau protein subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16772869", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16772869"}}, {start: {_id:3324}, end: {_id:2942}, properties:{evidence:"MAPK-activated protein kinase 2 (MK2) is one of several kinases that are regulated through direct phosphorylation by p38 MAPK, and MK2 has therefore been a candidate for an effector role in p38 action in the inflammatory response.æ¯�", annotationSubgraph:["Cytokine signaling subgraph", "MAPK-JNK subgraph"], pmid:"16774924", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16774924"}}, {start: {_id:2933}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Our data suggest that phosphorylation of tau by Akt may play specific role(s) in Akt-mediated anti-apoptotic signaling, particularly relevant to AD and other neurodegenerations.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Akt subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"14636947", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"14636947"}}, {start: {_id:2933}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"We have reported recently that the microtubule-associated protein tau is phosphorylated in vitro by Akt , an important kinase in anti- apoptotic signaling regulated by insulin and growth factors.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Akt subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"15283963", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"15283963"}}, {start: {_id:116}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Direct interaction of soluble human recombinant tau protein with Abeta 1-42 results in tau aggregation and hyperphosphorylation by tau protein kinase II.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Cyclin-CDK subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"11943163", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"11943163"}}, {start: {_id:3355}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Tau protein kinase I phosphorylated not only tau protein but also pyruvate dehydrogenase, phosphorylation of which caused inactivation of this enzyme and finally led the cell to death.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Disaccharide metabolism subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"20075608", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20075608"}}, {start: {_id:3355}, end: {_id:3356}, properties:{evidence:"Tau protein kinase I phosphorylated not only tau protein but also pyruvate dehydrogenase, phosphorylation of which caused inactivation of this enzyme and finally led the cell to death.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Disaccharide metabolism subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"20075608", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20075608"}}, {start: {_id:3355}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"When a primary culture of embryonic rat hippocampus was treated with 20 microM A beta, induction of TPKI, extensive phosphorylation of tau and then programmed cell death were observed, indicating that TPKI induced by A beta phosphorylates tau, followed by disruption of axonal transportation and finally cell death.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Axonal transport subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"9089387", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"9089387"}}, {start: {_id:3357}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Aberrant tau phosphorylation by glycogen synthase kinase-3beta and JNK3 induces oligomeric tau fibrils in COS-7 cells.", annotationSubgraph:["MAPK-JNK subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph", "Tau protein subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"12191990", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"12191990"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Aberrant tau phosphorylation by glycogen synthase kinase-3beta and JNK3 induces oligomeric tau fibrils in COS-7 cells.", annotationSubgraph:["MAPK-JNK subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph", "Tau protein subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"12191990", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"12191990"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"In the present review, we discuss our initial in vitro results and additional investigations showing that Abeta activates GSK-3beta through impairment of phosphatidylinositol-3 (PI3)/Akt signaling; that Abeta-activated GSK-3beta induces hyperphosphorylation of tau, NFT formation, neuronal death, and synaptic loss (all found in the AD brain); that GSK-3beta can induce memory deficits in vivo; and that inhibition of GSK-3alpha (an isoform of GSK-3beta) reduces Abeta production.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16914869", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16914869"}}, {start: {_id:123}, end: {_id:2617}, properties:{evidence:"In vitro phosphorylation of the cytoplasmic domain of the amyloid precursor protein by glycogen synthase kinase-3beta.", annotationSubgraph:["Amyloidogenic subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"8764598", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"8764598"}}, {start: {_id:211}, end: {_id:118}, properties:{evidence:"Several kinases, such as glycogen synthase kinase 3 beta (GSK3beta) and c-Jun N-terminal kinase (JNK), phosphorylate tau at sites that are phosphorylated in PHF.", annotationSubgraph:["MAPK-JNK subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph", "Tau protein subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"11803455", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"11803455"}}] AS row
