d Ser-404, but not at Thr-212; and (ii) with GSK-3beta at Thr-181, Ser-202, Thr-205, Ser-217, and Ser-404, but not at Ser-199, Thr-212, Thr-231, or Ser-396.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph", "Cyclin-CDK subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Low"], pmid:"12387894", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"12387894"}}, {start: {_id:122}, end: {_id:391}, properties:{evidence:"Interestingly, GPCs from AD patients exhibited elevated levels of glycogen synthase kinase 3beta (GSK-3beta, an enzyme known to phosphorylate beta-catenin), accompanied by an increase in phosphorylated beta-catenin and a decrease in nonphosphorylated beta- catenin compared with HC counterparts.", annotationSubgraph:["Beta-Catenin subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"19458225", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"19458225"}}, {start: {_id:996}, end: {_id:563}, properties:{evidence:"Both GSK-3alpha and 3beta phosphorylate purified pig brain CRMP-2 and significantly alter its mobility in SDS-gels, resembling the CRMP-2 pmodification observed in AD brain.", annotationSubgraph:["Nerve growth factor subgraph", "Axonal guidance subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph", "Regulation of actin cytoskeleton subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9823"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"17902168", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"17902168"}}, {start: {_id:122}, end: {_id:563}, properties:{evidence:"Both GSK-3alpha and 3beta phosphorylate purified pig brain CRMP-2 and significantly alter its mobility in SDS-gels, resembling the CRMP-2 pmodification observed in AD brain.", annotationSubgraph:["Nerve growth factor subgraph", "Axonal guidance subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph", "Regulation of actin cytoskeleton subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9823"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"17902168", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"17902168"}}, {start: {_id:6}, end: {_id:3074}, properties:{evidence:"In SH-SY5Y cells, results showed that Abeta42 induced a large increase in phosphorylated PKR and FADD le