e shown previously that activation of PKR in Abeta-triggered apoptotic process.", annotationSubgraph:["MAPK-JNK subgraph", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"16532272", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16532272"}}, {start: {_id:2339}, end: {_id:2340}, properties:{evidence:"In contrast, activation of ABCC1 using thiethylperazine (a drug approved by the FDA to relieve nausea and vomiting) markedly reduced Abeta load in a mouse model of AD expressing ABCC1 but not in such mice lacking ABCC1.", annotationSubgraph:["ATP binding cassette transport subgraph", "Non-amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["10090"], annotationMeshdisease:["Nausea", "Vomiting", "Alzheimer Disease"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"21881209", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21881209"}}, {start: {_id:1962}, end: {_id:2380}, properties:{evidence:"Serotonin hyperpolarizes entorhinal neurons and inhibits the excitatory synaptic transmission via activation of 5-HT(1A) receptors but facilitates GABA release via activation of 5-HT(2A) receptors.", annotationSubgraph:["Serotonergic subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Neurons"], pmid:"23320133", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23320133"}}, {start: {_id:1962}, end: {_id:2382}, properties:{evidence:"Serotonin hyperpolarizes entorhinal neurons and inhibits the excitatory synaptic transmission via activation of 5-HT(1A) receptors but facilitates GABA release via activation of 5-HT(2A) receptors.", annotationSubgraph:["Serotonergic subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Neurons"], pmid:"23320133", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23320133"}}, {start: {_id:2392}, end: {_id:457}, properties:{evidence:"Acrolein induces Hsp72 via both PKCdelta/JNK and calcium signaling pathways in human umbilical vein endothelial cells.", annotationSubgraph:["Phosphatidylinositol 3 subgraph", "JAK-STAT signaling subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9606"], annotationCell:["endothelial cell of umbilical vein"], pmid:"16036326", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16036326"}}, {start: {_id:2409}, end: {_id:2384}, properties:{evidence:"In cells treated with wortmannin, protein kinase C delta fragments were observed, and the protein kinase C activity increased after 3 hours, whereas treatment of cells with z-DEVD-fmk, an inhibitor of caspase-3, inhibited fragmentation of protein kinase C delta and induced continuous activation of GSK-3.", annotationSubgraph:["Phosphatidylinositol 3 subgraph", "Caspase subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"10850726", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"10850726"}}, {start: {_id:2410}, end: {_id:121}, properties:{evidence:"In cells treated with wortmannin, protein kinase C delta fragments were observed, and the protein kinase C activity increased after 3 hours, whereas treatment of cells with z-DEVD-fmk, an inhibitor of caspase-3, inhibited fragmentation of protein kinase C delta and induced continuous activation of GSK-3.", annotationSubgraph:["Phosphatidylinositol 3 subgraph", "Caspase subgraph", "GSK3 subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"10850726", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"10850726"}}, {start: {_id:328}, end: {_id:1292}, properties:{evidence:"Zinc-induced p70S6K activation could only upregulate translation of total S6 and tau but not global proteins in SH-SY5Y cells.", annotationSubgraph:["mTOR signaling subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"16364302", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"16364302"}}, {start: {_id:3}, end: {_id:1292}, properties:{evidence:"The extracellular amyloid-beta deposition in AD brains could be a causative factor that activates p70S6K. We hypothesized that amyloid- beta deposition activates p70S6K whose anti-apoptotic property subsequently keeps neurons from entering into the apoptotic process.", annotationSubgraph:["Amyloidogenic subgraph", "mTOR signaling subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Brain"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"18688088", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"18688088"}}, {start: {_id:1838}, end: {_id:2455}, properties:{evidence:"A significant (Pb0.01) increase in activity and mRNA expression of caspase-3 was observed in hippocampus, striatum and cortex of OKA treated rat brain in comparison to that of control and vehicle groups. Treatment with memantine and donepezil significantly (P<0.05) decreased caspase-3 activity and mRNA level in hippocampus, striatum and cortex of OKA 200 ng treated rat brain", annotationSubgraph:["Caspase subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["10116"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Hippocampus", "Cerebral Cortex"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"21893081", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21893081"}}, {start: {_id:1838}, end: {_id:2502}, properties:{evidence:"A significant (Pb0.01) increase in activity and mRNA expression of caspase-9 was observed in hippocampus and cortex of OKA treated rats as compared to that of control and vehicle group. Treatment with memantine and donepezil significantly (P<0.01) decreased caspase-9 activity and mRNA expression in hippocampus and cortex as compared to OKA 200 ng treated group (Fig. 10A and B).", annotationSubgraph:["Caspase subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["10116"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Hippocampus", "Cerebral Cortex"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"21893081", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21893081"}}, {start: {_id:93}, end: {_id:2517}, properties:{evidence:"We also examined a possible effect of CIIA on TRAF2-ASK1 interaction, because the recruitment of TRAF2 to ASK1 is an integral part of the mechanism for ROS-induced ASK1 activation. SOD1(G93A) induced the binding of TRAF2 to ASK1 in NSC34 cells and this binding was potentiated in those expressing a CIIA siRNA (Figure 2C, upper panel), suggesting that CIIA suppresses the SOD1(G93A)-induced TRAF2-ASK1 interaction.", annotationSpecies:["10090"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Neurons"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"25018698", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25018698"}}, {start: {_id:93}, end: {_id:2526}, properties:{evidence:"Furthermore, our data with ROS scavengers suggest that intracellular ROS mediates the SOD1(G93A)-induced activation of MST1, although the origin of ROS generation induced by SOD1(G93A) remains unclear (25).", annotationSubgraph:["Reactive oxygen species subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["10090"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"23818595", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23818595"}}, {start: {_id:93}, end: {_id:2544}, properties:{evidence:"Taken together, these results suggest that glucose deprivation leads to p53 activation through a pathway that involves elevated ROS levels and ATM activation in the absence of DNA double-strand breaks. In this paper, we report that glucose deprivation results in ROS production and in the activation of endogenous p53 through an ATM-dependent mechanism.", annotationSubgraph:["Reactive oxygen species subgraph", "Response DNA damage"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"22055193", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22055193"}}, {start: {_id:93}, end: {_id:562}, properties:{evidence:"Taken together, these results suggest that glucose deprivation leads to p53 activation through a pathway that involves elevated ROS levels and ATM activation in the absence of DNA double-strand breaks. In this paper, we report that glucose deprivation results in ROS production and in the activation of endogenous p53 through an ATM-dependent mechanism.", annotationSubgraph:["Reactive oxygen species subgraph", "Response DNA damage"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"22055193", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22055193"}}] AS row
