lt was observed in the APOE ε4 positive samples (Pâ€‰=â€‰0.06). SNP 20 from the ENPP1 gene (Gene ID 5167) showed evidence for association in both the APOE ε4 positive and ε4 negative samples. A final 7 SNPs showed evidence of association in the APOE ε4 positive samples, SNP 34 (INPPL1 Gene ID 3636), SNP 62 (HK2 Gene ID 3099), SNP 93 (NOS3 Gene ID 4846), and in the APOE ε4 negative samples, SNP 72 (GC Gene ID 2638), SNP 94 (ADRB3 Gene ID 155), SNP 130 (CETP Gene ID 1071), and SNP 136 (PPP2R1A Gene ID 5518). Following correction using the False Discovery Rate Procedure (FDR) at a variety of levels, however, the majority of these results could be rejected as false discoveries (Table S8).", annotationSubgraph:["Lipid metabolism subgraph", "Wnt signaling subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"19885299", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"19885299"}}, {start: {_id:1419}, end: {_id:27}, properties:{evidence:"ATXN1 functions as a genetic risk modifier that contributes to AD pathogenesis through a loss-of-function mechanism by regulating beta- secretase cleavage of APP and Abeta levels.", annotationSubgraph:["Beta secretase subgraph", "Akt subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"20097758", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20097758"}}, {start: {_id:856}, end: {_id:27}, properties:{evidence:"In a replication study, we confirmed significant association of SNPs within three genes--PPARgamma, SOS2, and PCK1--with Alzheimer's disease.", annotationSubgraph:["Peroxisome proliferator activated receptor subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"17440948", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"17440948"}}, {start: {_id:1165}, end: {_id:27}, properties:{evidence:"In a replication study, we confirmed significant association of SNPs within three genes--PPARgamma, SOS2, and PCK1--with Alzheimer's disease.", annotationSubgraph:["Regulation of actin cytoskeleton subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"17440