:"PubMed", citationRef:"21711233"}}, {start: {_id:2344}, end: {_id:2216}, properties:{evidence:"Qualitative and quantitative changes in the expressions of uPAR and of its canonical ligand uPA have been observed in a large variety of epileptic disorders, either in human or in animal models, as well as in other brain diseases (stroke and brain trauma, multiple sclerosis, Alzheimer's disease, cerebral malaria, HIV-associated leukoencephalopathy and encephalitis).", annotationSubgraph:["Plasminogen activator subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9606"], annotationMeshdisease:["Leukoencephalopathies", "Multiple Sclerosis", "Malaria, Cerebral", "Brain Injuries", "Stroke", "Encephalitis", "Brain Diseases", "Alzheimer Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Cerebrum", "Brain"], pmid:"21711233", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21711233"}}, {start: {_id:2344}, end: {_id:2346}, properties:{evidence:"Qualitative and quantitative changes in the expressions of uPAR and of its canonical ligand uPA have been observed in a large variety of epileptic disorders, either in human or in animal models, as well as in other brain diseases (stroke and brain trauma, multiple sclerosis, Alzheimer's disease, cerebral malaria, HIV-associated leukoencephalopathy and encephalitis).", annotationSubgraph:["Plasminogen activator subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9606"], annotationMeshdisease:["Leukoencephalopathies", "Multiple Sclerosis", "Malaria, Cerebral", "Brain Injuries", "Stroke", "Encephalitis", "Brain Diseases", "Alzheimer Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Cerebrum", "Brain"], pmid:"21711233", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21711233"}}] AS row
