minantly localized in hypothalamus, thymus, skeletal muscle, heart, kidney, and liver [26-28]. Upon its activation the IRS proteins bind several Src homology(SH)2 domainÂ­ containing cellular signaling proteins, such as p85, the reguÂ­ latory subunit of phosphatidylinositide(PI)3-kinase, growth factor receptor binding protein(G RB)2 and SH2-Phosphatase (SHP)2.", annotationSubgraph:["Insulin signal transduction"], annotationConfidence:["Medium"], pmid:"19519303", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"19519303"}}] AS row
