ase subunits IV and Vb proteins and was associated with decreased cytochrome oxidase and increased free radical production", annotationSubgraph:["Reactive oxygen species subgraph", "Electron transport chain", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"22523685", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22523685"}}, {start: {_id:304}, end: {_id:314}, properties:{annotationCellstructure:["Mitochondria"], evidence:"The accumulation of APP across mitochondrial import channels inhibited the entry of nuclear-encoded cytochrome c-oxidase subunits IV and Vb proteins and was associated with decreased cytochrome oxidase and increased free radical production", annotationSubgraph:["Reactive oxygen species subgraph", "Electron transport chain", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"22523685", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22523685"}}, {start: {_id:310}, end: {_id:314}, properties:{annotationCellstructure:["Mitochondria"], evidence:"The accumulation of APP across mitochondrial import channels inhibited the entry of nuclear-encoded cytochrome c-oxidase subunits IV and Vb proteins and was associated with decreased cytochrome oxidase and increased free radical production", annotationSubgraph:["Reactive oxygen species subgraph", "Electron transport chain", "Amyloidogenic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"22523685", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22523685"}}, {start: {_id:605}, end: {_id:604}, properties:{evidence:"Acetylcholinesterase (AChE) is thought to play an important role during apoptotic process. Our results showed that H2O2 induced AChE activity, a functional marker in apoptotic process, increases in neuronal-like PC12 cells. Glutathione, which is involved in cellular redox homeostasis, inhibited the increase of AChE activity, suggesting that reactive oxygen species (ROS) play a key role in this process. Further investigation showed that the elevation of AChE was observed after the degradation of Akt, release of cytochrome c from mitochondria into the cytosol, and activation of caspase family members. When nerve growth factor (NGF) was present, with the maintenance of Akt level, the elevation of AChE, the cytochrome c diffusion, as well as apoptotic process were markedly attenuated in H2O2-treated PC12 cells", annotationSubgraph:["Acetylcholine signaling subgraph", "Caspase subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"17213958", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"17213958"}}, {start: {_id:6}, end: {_id:711}, properties:{evidence:"The low-density lipoprotein receptor (LDLR) has the highest affinity for apoE and plays an important role in brain cholesterol metabolism.These data suggest that increased APP expression and Abeta exposure alters microtubule function, leading to reduced transport of LDLR to the plasma membrane. Consequent deleterious effects on apoE uptake and function will have implications for AD pathogenesis and/or progression", annotationSubgraph:["Cholesterol metabolism subgraph", "Low density lipoprotein subgraph", "APOE subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"20049331", annotationDisease:["Alzheimer's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20049331"}}] AS row
